1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,636
A sitemap lists the pages of your site in a form that search engines read.

2
00:00:05,636 --> 00:00:09,171
The Sitemaps module builds that list from your content.

3
00:00:09,171 --> 00:00:14,270
In this video, you create a sitemap, choose its content, and control single pages.

4
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:23,474
A sitemap is an XML document that lists the addresses of your pages.

5
00:00:23,474 --> 00:00:28,015
Each entry can also carry the date the page last changed, how often

6
00:00:28,015 --> 00:00:31,810
it changes, and its priority compared with other pages.

7
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:36,855
In Orchard Core, a sitemap has a name, a permalink that ends in

8
00:00:36,855 --> 00:00:39,034
.xml, and an Enabled setting.

9
00:00:39,034 --> 00:00:44,200
Browsing to the permalink shows the sitemap, which is built from its sources.

10
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:47,569
A source decides what the sitemap lists.

11
00:00:47,569 --> 00:00:52,353
Sitemap Content Types lists the content items of the content types you choose.

12
00:00:52,353 --> 00:00:55,940
Sitemap Custom Path lists a single address that you type.

13
00:01:00,155 --> 00:01:03,074
Sitemaps is a feature that you enable.

14
00:01:03,074 --> 00:01:08,845
Open Tools, Features, search for Sitemaps, and enable the feature named Sitemaps.

15
00:01:09,302 --> 00:01:13,591
Its pages appear under Tools, Search Engine Optimization:

16
00:01:13,591 --> 00:01:17,131
Sitemaps, Sitemap Indexes, and Sitemaps Cache.

17
00:01:17,131 --> 00:01:18,492
Open Sitemaps.

18
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:22,605
A warning says the Base url setting is empty.

19
00:01:22,605 --> 00:01:28,410
Every address in a sitemap starts with the Base url, so a sitemap needs it.

20
00:01:28,868 --> 00:01:30,861
Open Settings, General.

21
00:01:30,861 --> 00:01:34,915
Enter the address of your site in Base url, and save.

22
00:01:34,915 --> 00:01:37,938
Sitemaps use it to build each address.

23
00:01:42,221 --> 00:01:44,813
On the Sitemaps page, choose Add Sitemap.

24
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:45,806
Type a Name.

25
00:01:45,806 --> 00:01:47,791
Let's call this sitemap Pages.

26
00:01:48,262 --> 00:01:53,620
Permalink is the address where the sitemap is served, after the Base url.

27
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:58,842
Leave it empty, and the module builds it from the name, ending in .xml.

28
00:01:59,309 --> 00:02:00,677
Enabled is checked.

29
00:02:00,677 --> 00:02:04,835
If you uncheck it, the module stops serving the sitemap, but keeps it.

30
00:02:04,835 --> 00:02:05,929
Choose Create.

31
00:02:06,452 --> 00:02:09,896
The sitemap appears in the list with an Enabled badge.

32
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:14,775
Its buttons manage the sources, view the sitemap, edit its name, permalink, and

33
00:02:14,775 --> 00:02:16,842
Enabled setting, or delete it.

34
00:02:21,082 --> 00:02:24,269
A sitemap lists nothing until it has a source.

35
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:27,272
Choose Manage Sources, and then Add Source.

36
00:02:27,724 --> 00:02:32,693
Available Sources offers Sitemap Content Types and Sitemap Custom Path.

37
00:02:32,693 --> 00:02:35,404
Choose Add on Sitemap Content Types.

38
00:02:35,881 --> 00:02:38,203
Index All Content Types is checked.

39
00:02:38,203 --> 00:02:42,962
The sitemap then lists every published content item whose content type has the

40
00:02:42,962 --> 00:02:46,701
Autoroute part, because Autoroute gives an item its address.

41
00:02:47,155 --> 00:02:51,261
Change Frequency and Priority are the defaults for these entries.

42
00:02:51,261 --> 00:02:55,423
Priority runs from zero to one, and ranks a page against the other

43
00:02:55,423 --> 00:02:56,869
pages of your site.

44
00:02:56,869 --> 00:02:58,025
Choose Create.

45
00:02:58,487 --> 00:03:01,058
The source is listed with the badge All.

46
00:03:01,058 --> 00:03:04,747
The sitemap serves an entry for each of those content items.

47
00:03:08,998 --> 00:03:10,089
Choose View.

48
00:03:10,089 --> 00:03:14,328
The sitemap opens in another tab, at its permalink on your site.

49
00:03:14,818 --> 00:03:19,221
Each content item has an entry with its address and, when it has

50
00:03:19,221 --> 00:03:21,359
one, its last modified date.

51
00:03:21,359 --> 00:03:25,448
The change frequency and the priority come from the source.

52
00:03:29,654 --> 00:03:34,122
To list only some types, go back to Manage Sources, choose Edit on

53
00:03:34,122 --> 00:03:37,474
the source, and uncheck Index All Content Types.

54
00:03:37,929 --> 00:03:40,022
A list of content types appears.

55
00:03:40,022 --> 00:03:43,327
Only content types with the Autoroute part are listed.

56
00:03:43,327 --> 00:03:45,199
Check Article and Blog Post.

57
00:03:45,655 --> 00:03:49,894
Each checked type has its own Change Frequency and Priority.

58
00:03:49,894 --> 00:03:54,839
Set Blog Post to Weekly with a higher priority, and Article to Monthly.

59
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:56,315
Then choose Save.

60
00:03:56,767 --> 00:03:59,866
The source shows a badge for each selected type.

61
00:03:59,866 --> 00:04:05,147
Viewing the sitemap again lists only articles and blog posts, with the values you set.

62
00:04:09,338 --> 00:04:13,358
The Tags page of this site is not in the sitemap, because the

63
00:04:13,358 --> 00:04:15,998
source selects only two content types.

64
00:04:15,998 --> 00:04:19,658
Choose Add Source, and then Add on Sitemap Custom Path.

65
00:04:20,113 --> 00:04:21,978
Type tags as the Path.

66
00:04:21,978 --> 00:04:25,643
The hint shows the format, with no leading slash.

67
00:04:25,643 --> 00:04:30,173
A path cannot contain spaces, dots, or most other punctuation.

68
00:04:30,626 --> 00:04:34,090
Set Change Frequency to Monthly, and choose Create.

69
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:38,646
The source is listed with its path and the label Sitemap Custom Path.

70
00:04:39,101 --> 00:04:44,211
Viewing the sitemap shows the Tags address next to the articles and blog posts.

71
00:04:48,414 --> 00:04:52,903
To control a single page, add the Sitemap part to its content type.

72
00:04:52,903 --> 00:04:56,408
A part adds its settings to every item of the type.

73
00:04:56,408 --> 00:05:00,774
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit Article.

74
00:05:01,225 --> 00:05:05,357
Choose Add Parts, check Sitemap, and choose Add Selected Parts.

75
00:05:05,357 --> 00:05:08,291
Content items are listed without this part.

76
00:05:08,291 --> 00:05:11,525
It lets a single item be excluded or configured.

77
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:15,660
Open Content, Content Items, and edit the About article.

78
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,392
The Sitemap settings are on the SEO tab.

79
00:05:18,392 --> 00:05:21,718
Check Override sitemap configuration to show them.

80
00:05:22,174 --> 00:05:25,954
Exclude removes this item from the sitemaps that list it.

81
00:05:25,954 --> 00:05:30,934
Change Frequency and Priority replace the source's values for this item only.

82
00:05:30,934 --> 00:05:33,334
Check Exclude, and choose Publish.

83
00:05:33,794 --> 00:05:37,403
Publishing makes the sitemap build again on its next view.

84
00:05:37,403 --> 00:05:39,263
View it, and About is gone.

85
00:05:39,263 --> 00:05:43,944
Items that do not override the configuration keep the values of their source.

86
00:05:48,144 --> 00:05:52,396
When the SEO feature is enabled, the site serves a robots file.

87
00:05:52,396 --> 00:05:56,094
If the site has no robots file of its own and the Base

88
00:05:56,094 --> 00:06:01,394
url is set, the module can list your enabled sitemaps and sitemap indexes in it.

89
00:06:02,144 --> 00:06:06,097
It does so once Include all sitemaps is checked and saved.

90
00:06:06,097 --> 00:06:11,472
You find that setting under Settings, Search, Search Engine Optimization, Robots.

91
00:06:11,472 --> 00:06:14,314
A separate video covers the robots file.

92
00:06:16,314 --> 00:06:20,581
You created a sitemap, chose what it lists, and controlled single pages.

93
00:06:20,581 --> 00:06:22,004
Thanks for watching.

